  "title": "The Horse in Motion — Sallie Gardner at a Gallop",
  "kind": "animation",
  "status": "published",
  "summary": "Leland Stanford's mare Sallie Gardner galloping at Palo Alto track, proving all four hooves leave the ground simultaneously.",
  "description": "Captured in June 1878 at the Palo Alto Stock Farm using a battery of 24 cameras with electro-magnetic shutter releases triggered by tripwires. Published in 1881 as 'The Attitudes of Animals in Motion'. One of the foundational achievements in the history of high-speed photography and moving images.",
